WEBVTT

00:03:26.702 --> 00:03:30.915
so brothers, nephews, and uncles 
fought to gain power.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:36.963
Within the court, army officers, wives, 
concubines, and government officials

00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:39.423
all demanded their share of the treasury.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.511
Because the caliph depended 
on his entourage to stay in power,

00:03:43.761 --> 00:03:48.474
each transition of rulership opened
the doors for favoritism and corruption.

00:03:48.641 --> 00:03:49.934
Outside the court,

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.770
many questioned the legitimacy
of the caliph,

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.232
noting that the caliph’s religious duty
to moral excellence

00:03:56.232 --> 00:03:59.318
was at odds with the court’s 
decadent displays of wealth.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:03.698
In 1258 CE, the Mongols
approached Baghdad.